WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.102
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.637
SPEAKER: It's in all of us...

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:09.242
 that fear of being hurt...

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.245
because we're queer.

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:14.413
♪ (DISCO MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:14.513 --> 00:00:18.151
Thank you, New York,
for being so fabulous.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:21.788
SPEAKER: I remember the first
 gay bar I walked into,

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.555
I thought, "Oh, my god,
I've been missing this

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.426
 my entire life."
 It just felt like home.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.895
SPEAKER 2: Queer bars were one
 of the few places

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.864
where we could come
and feel safe.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.866
SPEAKER 3:
 And then, all of a sudden...

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.001
-♪ (MUSIC ENDS ABRUPTLY)
 -everything was taken away.

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:39.305
SPEAKER 4:
 Dismembered human remains
 were found in plastic bags

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.640
 along roadways
 outside New York City.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.543
SPEAKER 5: My dad went down
 to New York

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:48.781
on a business trip
and never came home.

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:50.850
-SPEAKER 6: My brother.
-My uncle.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.853
-SPEAKER 7: My friend.
-SPEAKER 8: He just disappeared.

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.555
SPEAKER 9:
 These were pick up crimes.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.724
 They were last seen
 at a gay bar.

00:00:58.824 --> 00:00:59.792
 5 Oaks, the Townhouse.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:03.529
Clearly, a serial murderer
going after gay men

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:04.530
 was on the loose.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:08.968
SPEAKER 3:
 It was so frightening
 'cause everyone was a suspect.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.271
 The queer community
 was very much trying to

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:15.275
push law enforcement
to give a shit.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.910
At this time,
we wouldn't put it past

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.246
-the police to kill us.
-♪ (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.915
SPEAKER 10: Hate crimes
 against gays and lesbians

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:24.483
 are up all over the country.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.219
Makes people feel like
maybe they're not safe

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.687
and maybe a murderer
isn't gonna get caught.

00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:31.991
SPEAKER 3: We were scared.
This guy is gonna strike again,

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.593
and could I be next?

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:36.762
 -Peter Anderson.
-SPEAKER 11: Thomas Mulcahy.

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:38.731
-SPEAKER 12: Anthony Marrero.
-SPEAKER 13: Michael Sakara.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.467
They weren't just a statistic.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.635
 They had their own story too.

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:46.138
This guy was
a serial killer for years.

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:48.507
SPEAKER 14:
 Was he gonna make a mistake?

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.611
How does someone get away
with something like that?

